{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Mobile: space fixes for the cart drawer.

  1. The "Your Cart (n items)" bar stops sticking.
     pg-drawer pins it with `.pg-cart-top{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:6}`. It
     permanently eats part of the panel and rides over whatever scrolls beneath
     it -- on a phone it sat on top of the "Add & Save More" heading, on desktop
     it covers the drawer logo and free-shipping pill. It now scrolls with the
     list, keeping its background and rule so it still reads as the panel header.

  2. The strip of cart peeking out under the pane is painted over.
     The drawer carries an inline `padding-bottom` written by the theme's own
     script -- 34px in Safari, inline and !important, so no stylesheet can
     override it -- while the pane sticks at `bottom:-10px`. The pane therefore
     comes to rest short of the bottom edge, and the cart list shows through
     the difference as a strip of product under the checkout button.

     It is covered with a solid downward box-shadow rather than by moving the
     pane. A shadow paints but does not lay out: it cannot push anything off
     screen, and `#cart`'s own `overflow:hidden auto` clips it to the drawer.
     The spread is deliberately far larger than the 24px it needs to cover, so
     it still works wherever that padding is bigger.

     DO NOT go back to repositioning the pane to close this gap. Pulling it
     down by the measured padding (`bottom:-Npx`) works in Safari and breaks
     the Instagram in-app browser: that webview has a tall bottom toolbar, so
     the padding is far larger there, and shifting the pane by it pushed the
     savings box, the Total, the trust row and the CHECKOUT button clean off
     the bottom of the screen. Shoppers arriving from an Instagram ad reached
     the cart and had no way to check out.

  3. The pane gets shorter under 760px.
     `.sticky-in-panel` stacks shipping protection, the savings breakdown, the
     totals, the trust row, the checkout button and the payment icons. Each is
     fine on its own; together they take more than half a phone screen.

     Everything is tightened: smaller paddings and gaps, and one step down in
     type on the secondary rows. The shipping-protection subtitle ("Protect
     your order against loss or damage in transit") is hidden below 760px --
     the label, price and toggle all remain, and that sentence is a full
     wrapped line on a phone.

     The total and the checkout button are deliberately left large: they are
     what the pane is for.

  4. The payment-icon row is dropped from the pane at every width (below).

  5. The upsell card moves down on mobile only.
     `.pg-unlock` ("Add your FREE 3rd Crystal PokeOrb") renders above the cart
     itself, so on a phone the first thing in the drawer is an offer and the
     items you actually added are pushed off the bottom of the screen. It is
     moved to sit immediately before the pinned pane, which puts it directly
     above Shipping Protection -- last thing before the totals, next to the
     checkout button, where it reads as an add-on rather than a wall in front
     of the cart. Desktop keeps it where it was; the drawer has the height.

  NOT DONE, deliberately: unpinning the pane entirely. It was tried and it
  turned the drawer blank on iOS Safari -- scrolled to the top, the panel
  painted white with no content, though the markup and computed colours were
  correct. Removing the sticky element drops a compositing layer from a
  position:fixed, internally-scrolling container, which iOS is known to render
  as unpainted white. The pane stays pinned for that reason. If more room for
  the item list is wanted, pin a slim bar (total + checkout only) and let the
  rest of the pane scroll, rather than unpinning the whole thing.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
/* 1. header bar scrolls away, all widths */
#cart .pg-cart-top{
  position:static !important;
  top:auto !important;
  z-index:auto !important
}

/* 4. the payment-icon row comes out of the pinned pane, all widths.
   It is a wrapped strip of card-brand logos plus its own margins sitting
   directly under the checkout button, and it is permanently on screen because
   the pane is pinned -- so it costs that height on every drawer, at every
   scroll position, to say something the "SECURE CHECKOUT" line above it
   already says. The accepted cards are still shown at checkout itself and in
   the site footer. Scoped to the pane so the footer's own strip is untouched
   (`#cart .sticky-in-panel .l4pm` outranks pg-drawer's `#cart .l4pm`). */
#cart .sticky-in-panel .l4pm{display:none !important}

/* 2. paint over the strip of cart showing below the pane, all widths.
   First shadow is pg-drawer's original lift above the pane; the second is a
   solid block of the pane's own white running downwards, with no blur and no
   layout effect. 400px is far more than the gap needs -- it just has to
   outlast the drawer's bottom padding on any browser -- and the drawer clips
   it. See the note at the top before changing this. */
#cart .sticky-in-panel{
  box-shadow:0 -14px 26px -18px rgba(74,28,102,.4), 0 400px 0 0 #fff !important
}

@media (max-width:760px){
  /* 3. compact the pane */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel{padding-top:3px !important}

  /* shipping protection: single line, smaller icon */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp{margin:2px 0 5px !important;padding:6px 9px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-ic{width:24px !important;height:24px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-ic svg{width:14px !important;height:14px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t b{font-size:12.5px !important;line-height:1.25 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t small{display:none !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-price{font-size:12.5px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-sw{transform:scale(.9);transform-origin:right center}

  /* savings breakdown */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sav{margin:2px 0 5px !important;padding:6px 9px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sav-r{font-size:12px !important;line-height:1.4 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sav-t{margin-top:3px !important;padding-top:4px !important;font-size:12.5px !important}

  /* totals: subtotal and discount rows tighten, the Total holds its weight */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt{margin:1px 0 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li{font-size:12.5px !important;padding:0 !important;line-height:1.35 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-drow,#cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-drow *{font-size:12.5px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-tt,#cart .sticky-in-panel .l4tt li.pg-tt *{font-size:15px !important}

  /* trust strip */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .nc-dtrust{margin:2px 0 !important;padding:0 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .nc-dtrust span{font-size:10px !important}

  /* checkout stays a full-size target */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel form.f8vl{margin:2px 0 0 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel button[name="checkout"]{padding:12px 16px !important}
}
</style>
<script>
/* 5. move the upsell card on phones. Nothing here repositions the pane -- see
   the note at the top of this file. */
(function(){
  if (window.pgCartFlush) return; window.pgCartFlush = 1;

  /* 5. on phones, drop the upsell card down to just above the pinned pane, so
     it sits directly above Shipping Protection instead of in front of the
     cart. The position check is what makes this safe to run from a
     MutationObserver: once the card is already the pane's previous sibling
     there is nothing to do, so moving it cannot feed itself. */
  function placeUnlock(){
    var drawer = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!drawer) return;
    var card = drawer.querySelector('.pg-unlock');
    if (!card) return;

    if (window.matchMedia('(max-width:760px)').matches){
      var pane = drawer.querySelector('.sticky-in-panel');
      if (!pane || pane.previousElementSibling === card) return;
      /* remember the original slot so a resize up to desktop can undo this */
      if (!card.pgHome) card.pgHome = {parent: card.parentNode, next: card.nextSibling};
      pane.parentNode.insertBefore(card, pane);
    } else if (card.pgHome && card.pgHome.parent && card.pgHome.parent.isConnected){
      var home = card.pgHome;
      if (card.parentNode !== home.parent || card.nextSibling !== home.next){
        home.parent.insertBefore(card, home.next && home.next.isConnected ? home.next : null);
      }
    }
  }

  /* 6. CHECKOUT WATCHDOG.
     From a cold session -- which is every shopper arriving from an ad -- the
     page is served with an empty cart, so the drawer is rendered in its empty
     state. Adding to cart injects the line items client-side but the drawer is
     never re-rendered from the server, and the totals, the trust row and the
     CHECKOUT button only exist in the server's non-empty render. The result is
     a cart full of product with no way to buy it. `window.pgDrawerRefresh()`
     does not repair it (called directly, nothing changes); a full page load
     does.

     This re-fetches the current page and lifts the server's freshly rendered
     #cart into place -- the same trick pgDrawerRefresh is meant to do. It only
     runs in the broken state: items present AND no checkout button. A healthy
     drawer is never touched, so this costs nothing once the underlying bug is
     fixed, and it can be deleted then. */
  var repairing = false, lastRepair = 0;
  function repairCheckout(){
    var drawer = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!drawer || repairing) return;
    if (!drawer.querySelector('.l4ca > li')) return;            /* empty cart */
    if (drawer.querySelector('button[name="checkout"]')) return; /* healthy */
    if (Date.now() - lastRepair < 4000) return;                  /* don't spin */

    repairing = true;
    fetch(location.pathname + (location.search || ''), {credentials: 'same-origin'})
      .then(function(r){ return r.ok ? r.text() : null; })
      .then(function(html){
        if (!html) return;
        var fresh = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html').getElementById('cart');
        /* only swap in a render that actually has the button, so a cached or
           still-empty response can never make things worse */
        if (fresh && fresh.querySelector('button[name="checkout"]')){
          drawer.innerHTML = fresh.innerHTML;
          lastRepair = Date.now();
          placeUnlock();
        }
      })
      .catch(function(){})
      .then(function(){ repairing = false; });
  }

  function apply(){ placeUnlock(); repairCheckout(); }

  function boot(){
    apply();
    window.addEventListener('resize', apply);
    /* The pane only exists once the cart has something in it, and the theme
       replaces the drawer contents wholesale on every add, remove and quantity
       change -- a fresh upsell card each time, back in its original slot.
       Timers alone lose that race (an add-to-cart round trip outruns them), so
       watch for the re-render and re-apply. childList only. */
    if (window.MutationObserver){
      var queued = false;
      new MutationObserver(function(){
        if (queued) return;
        queued = true;
        setTimeout(function(){ queued = false; apply(); }, 60);
      }).observe(document.body, {childList:true, subtree:true});
    }
    [400, 1000, 2200, 4500].forEach(function(t){ setTimeout(apply, t); });
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot);
  else boot();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Mobile", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
